{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "John in Brazil", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Natural Wonders of Brazil", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Nature Around Us > Rainforest", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Continuous Tense  vs.  the Present Simple Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Present Simple tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul>  \t<li>things in general </li> \t<li>things that happen regularly </li> \t<li>things that do not change</li></ul>   \t\t\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form: subject + verb ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul>  \t<li>something that is happening now </li> \t<li>something that is happening around now (today) plans </li>  </ul>   \t\t\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form : subject + to be + verb+ing", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Present Simple </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I like cookies!<br /> He always wins that game!<br /> She enjoys dancing.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She's eating a cookie.<br /> He isn't winning today.<br /> They are dancing in the parade.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Zero Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the zero conditional to talk about general truths.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If this continues, the rainforest may disappear soon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One part is the condition. The other part is the result.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " From:<br />If + the Simple Present tense, the Simple Present Tense<br /> <span class=\"italic\">If I have time, I go to the cinema.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The condition is  <span class=\"italic\">have time</span>.  The result is go to the <span class=\"italic\">cinema</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Condition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Result </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you want to see the rainforest up close,<br /><br />  If you like trees and flowers,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">go with a group. <br /><br />  the rainforest is the place to visit!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " If too many trees are cut down, deserts can form. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you want to help, have a rainforest night.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Carnival ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a celebration in many countries ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I go to Brazil for Carnival every year!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you need to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "parade ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a special event when people walk or ride  n the same direction ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are thousands of people in the Carnival parade.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "samba ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dance from Brazil ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Everyone dances the samba at this club.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "spectacular ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "exciting and interesting ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The costumes are spectacular!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rainforest ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a forest in a hot area that has a lot of rain ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Amazon is the most important rainforest in the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to tap ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put a hole in a tree and let the sap out  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They tap the trees to get the sap from them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online to a Help the Rainforest site.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down 3 things people can do to help the rainforest.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Bring your ideas to class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read them to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I do research on problems in the rainforest", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down ways to save rainforests.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss my ideas about rainforest problems and solutions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn4le06ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "7000", "id": 1, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Vanessa?<br/>\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: John! How is the job going?<br />\n<span class =